#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1093
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scripting with JavaScript"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1095
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Since &kappname; 3.4 in KDE 4.4 the &kappname; editor component is easily extensible by writing scripts. The scripting language is ECMAScript (widely known as JavaScript). &kappname; supports two kinds of scripts: indentation and command line scripts."
msgid "The &kappname; editor component is easily extensible by writing scripts. The scripting language is ECMAScript (widely known as JavaScript). &kappname; supports two kinds of scripts: indentation and command line scripts."
msgstr "Desde a versión 3.4 de &kappname;, incluída na versión 4.4 da colección de software de KDE, pode ampliarse a funcionalidade do compoñente de edición de &kappname; mediante scripts. A linguaxe a empregar para estes scripts é ECMAScript (máis coñecida como JavaScript). &kappname; permite dous tipos de scripts: de sangrado e da liña de ordes."

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1102
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indentation Scripts"
msgstr "Scripts de sangrado"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1104
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Indentation scripts - also referred as indenters - automatically indent the source code while typing text. As example, after hitting the return-key code the indentation level often increases."
msgid "Indentation scripts - also referred as indenters - automatically indent the source code while typing text. As an example, after hitting the return key the indentation level often increases."
msgstr "Os scripts de sangrado axustan o sangrado do código fonte a medida que se escribe. Por exemplo, despois de premer a tecla Intro adoita aumentarse o nivel de sangrado."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1110
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "The following sections describe step by step how to create the skeleton for a simple indenter. As first step, create a new <filename>*.js</filename> file called e.g. <filename>javascript.js</filename> in the local home folder <filename>$KDEHOME/share/apps/katepart/script</filename>."
msgid "The following sections describe step by step how to create the skeleton for a simple indenter. As a first step, create a new <filename>*.js</filename> file called &eg; <filename>javascript.js</filename> in the local home folder <filename>$<envar>XDG_DATA_HOME</envar>/katepart5/script/indentation</filename>. Therein, the environment variable <envar>XDG_DATA_HOME</envar> typically expands to either <filename>~/.local</filename> or <filename>~/.local/share</filename>."
msgstr "As seguintes seccións describen paso a paso como crear o esqueleto dun script de sangrado sinxelo. O primeiro paso consistirá en crear un ficheiro <filename>*.js</filename> —por exemplo, <filename>javascript.js</filename>— no cartafol <filename>$KDEHOME/share/apps/katepart/script</filename>."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1118 development.docbook:1208
#, no-c-format
msgid "On &Windows; these files are located in <filename>%USERPROFILE%\\AppData\\Local\\katepart5\\indentation</filename>. <replaceable>%USERPROFILE%</replaceable> usually expands to <filename>C:\\\\Users\\\\<replaceable>user</replaceable></filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1122
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Indentation Script Header"
msgstr "Cabeceira"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1123
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "The header of the file <filename>javascript.js</filename> is embedded in a comment and is of the following form <programlisting>\n"
#| "/* kate-script\n"
#| " * name: JavaScript\n"
#| " * author: Example Name &lt;example.name@some.address.org&gt;\n"
#| " * license: BSD\n"
#| " * revision: 1\n"
#| " * kate-version: 3.4\n"
#| " * type: indentation\n"
#| " * required-syntax-style: javascript\n"
#| " * indent-languages: javascript\n"
#| " * priority: 0\n"
#| " * i18n-catalog: mycatalog\n"
#| " *\n"
#| " * A line without colon ':' stops header parsing. That is, you can add optional\n"
#| " * text here such as a detailed license.\n"
#| " */\n"
#| "</programlisting> Each entry is explained in detail now:"
msgid ""
"The header of the file <filename>javascript.js</filename> is embedded as JSON at the beginning of the document as follows: <programlisting>\n"
"var katescript = {\n"
"    \"name\": \"JavaScript\",\n"
"    \"author\": \"Example Name &lt;example.name@some.address.org&gt;\",\n"
"    \"license\": \"BSD License\",\n"
"    \"revision\": 1,\n"
"    \"kate-version\": \"5.1\",\n"
"    \"required-syntax-style\": \"javascript\",\n"
"    \"indent-languages\": [\"javascript\"],\n"
"    \"priority\": 0,\n"
"}; // kate-script-header, must be at the start of the file without comments\n"
"</programlisting> Each entry is explained in detail now:"
msgstr ""
"A cabeceira do ficheiro <filename>javascript.js</filename> escríbese nun comentario e ten a seguinte forma: <programlisting>\n"
"/* kate-script\n"
" * name: JavaScript\n"
" * author: Rosalía de Castro &lt;rosaliadecastro@example.com&gt;\n"
" * license: BSD\n"
" * revision: 1\n"
" * kate-version: 3.4\n"
" * type: indentation\n"
" * required-syntax-style: javascript\n"
" * indent-languages: javascript\n"
" * priority: 0\n"
" * i18n-catalog: catálogo_persoal\n"
" *\n"
" * A partir da primeira liña sen dous puntos («:») remata a análise\n"
" * da cabeceira, polo que pode empregar o comentario para\n"
" * texto adicional, como por exemplo detalles sobre a licencia\n"
" * do script.\n"
" */\n"
"</programlisting> A continuación explícanse punto por punto todas as entradas definidas na cabeceira:"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1130
#, no-c-format
msgid "<literal>name</literal> [required]: This is the indenter name that appears in the menu <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Indentation</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and in the configuration dialog."
msgstr "<literal>name</literal> (obrigatorio). Este é o nome do script de sangrado, o que aparecerá no menú <menuchoice><guimenu>Utilidades</guimenu><guimenuitem>Sangrado</guimenuitem></menuchoice> e no diálogo de configuración."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1135 development.docbook:1258
#, no-c-format
msgid "<literal>author</literal> [optional]: The author's name and contact information."
msgstr "<literal>author</literal> (opcional). O nome de autor e a información de contacto."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1138
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "<literal>license</literal> [optional]: Short form of the license, such as BSD or LGPLv3."
msgid "<literal>license</literal> [optional]: Short form of the license, such as BSD License or LGPLv3."
msgstr "<literal>license</literal> (opcional). Abreviatura da licenza. Por exemplo: BSD ou LGPLv3."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1141 development.docbook:1260
#, no-c-format
msgid "<literal>revision</literal> [required]: The revision of the script. This number should be increased whenever the script is modified."
msgstr "<literal>revision</literal> (obrigatorio). O número de revisión do script. Este número debería aumentarse cada vez que se modifique o script."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1144 development.docbook:1261
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "<literal>kate-version</literal> [required]: Minimal required &kappname; version."
msgid "<literal>kate-version</literal> [required]: Minimum required &kappname; version."
msgstr "<literal>kate-version</literal> (obrigatorio). A versión mínima de &kappname; necesaria para empregar o script."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1147
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "<literal>required-syntax-style</literal> [optional]: Comma separated list of required syntax highlighting styles. This is important for indenters that rely on specific highlight information in the document. If a required syntax style is specified, the indenter is available only when the appropriate highlighter is active. This prevents <quote>undefined behavior</quote> caused by using the indenter without the expected highlighting schema. For instance, the Ruby indenter makes use of this in the files <filename>ruby.js</filename> and <filename>ruby.xml</filename>."
msgid "<literal>required-syntax-style</literal> [optional]: The required syntax style, which matches the specified <literal>style</literal> in syntax highlighting files. This is important for indenters that rely on specific highlight information in the document. If a required syntax style is specified, the indenter is available only when the appropriate highlighter is active. This prevents <quote>undefined behavior</quote> caused by using the indenter without the expected highlighting schema. For instance, the Ruby indenter makes use of this in the files <filename>ruby.js</filename> and <filename>ruby.xml</filename>."
msgstr "<literal>required-syntax-style</literal> (opcional). Lista, separada por comas, de estilos de realzado de sintaxe que o script necesita. Isto é importante para aqueles scripts que dependen de información de realzado específica no documento. De indicarse un estilo de sintaxe necesario, o script de sangrado só estará dispoñíbel cando ese script de realzado estea activo. Así se evitan <quote>comportamentos inesperados</quote>, causados polo uso de scripts de sangrado sen o esquema de realzado do que estes dependen. Por exemplo, o script de sangrado de Ruby emprega esta opción nos ficheiros <filename>ruby.js</filename> e <filename>ruby.xml</filename>."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1150
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "<literal>indent-languages</literal> [optional]: Comma separated list of syntax styles the indenter can indent correctly, e.g.: c++, java."
msgid "<literal>indent-languages</literal> [optional]: JSON array of syntax styles the indenter can indent correctly, &eg;: <literal>[\"c++\", \"java\"]</literal>."
msgstr "<literal>indent-languages</literal> (opcional). Lista, separada por comas, de estilos de realzado que o script pode sangrar correctamente. Por exemplo: c++, java."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1153
#, no-c-format
msgid "<literal>priority</literal> [optional]: If several indenters are suited for a certain highlighted file, the priority decides which indenter is chosen as default indenter."
msgstr "<literal>priority</literal> (opcional). Se existen varios scripts de sangrado axeitados para un ficheiro de realzado concreto, o valor desta opción, a prioridade, determina cal dos scripts de sangrado se escolle de maneira predeterminada."

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1162
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Indenter Source Code"
msgstr "Código"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1163
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Having specified the header this section explains how the indentation scripting itself works. The basic skeleton of the body looks like this: <programlisting>\n"
#| "triggerCharacters = \"{}/:;\";\n"
#| "function indent(line, indentWidth, ch)\n"
#| "{\n"
#| "    // called for each newline (ch == '\\n') and all characters specified in\n"
#| "    // the global variable triggerCharacters. When calling <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Align</guimenuitem></menuchoice>\n"
#| "    // the variable ch is empty, i.e. ch == ''.\n"
#| "    //\n"
#| "    // see also: Scripting API\n"
#| "    return -2;\n"
#| "}\n"
#| "</programlisting> The function <function>indent()</function> has three parameters: "
#| "<itemizedlist> "
#| "<listitem>"
#| "<para><literal>line</literal>: the line that has to be indented</para>"
#| "</listitem>"
#| " "
#| "<listitem>"
#| "<para><literal>indentWidth</literal>: the indentation width in amount of spaces</para>"
#| "</listitem>"
#| " "
#| "<listitem>"
#| "<para><literal>ch</literal>: either a newline character (<literal>ch == '\\n'</literal>), the trigger character specified in <literal>triggerCharacters</literal> or empty if the user invoked the action <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Align</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.</para>"
#| "</listitem>"
#| " </itemizedlist>"
#| " The return value of the <function>indent()</function> function specifies how the line will be indented. If the return value is a simple integer number, it is interpreted as follows: "
#| "<itemizedlist> "
#| "<listitem>"
#| "<para>return value <literal>-2</literal>: do nothing</para>"
#| "</listitem>"
#| " "
#| "<listitem>"
#| "<para>return value <literal>-1</literal>: keep indentation (searches for previous non-blank line)</para>"
#| "</listitem>"
#| " "
#| "<listitem>"
#| "<para>return value <literal> 0</literal>: numbers &gt;= 0 specify the indentation depth in spaces</para>"
#| "</listitem>"
#| " </itemizedlist>"
#| " Alternatively, an array of two elements can be returned: "
#| "<itemizedlist> "
#| "<listitem>"
#| "<para><literal>return [ indent, align ];</literal></para>"
#| "</listitem>"
#| " </itemizedlist>"
#| " In this case, the first element is the indentation depth like above with the same meaning of the special values. However, the second element is an absolute value representing a column for <quote>alignment</quote>. If this value is higher than the indent value, the difference represents a number of spaces to be added after the indentation of the first parameter. Otherwise, the second number is ignored. Using tabs and spaces for indentation is often referred to as <quote>mixed mode</quote>."
msgid ""
"Having specified the header this section explains how the indentation scripting itself works. The basic skeleton of the body looks like this: <programlisting>\n"
"// required katepart js libraries, e.g. range.js if you use Range\n"
"require (\"range.js\");\n"
"\n"
"triggerCharacters = \"{}/:;\";\n"
"function indent(line, indentWidth, ch)\n"
"{\n"
"    // called for each newline (ch == '\\n') and all characters specified in\n"
"    // the global variable triggerCharacters. When calling <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Align</guimenuitem></menuchoice>\n"
"    // the variable ch is empty, i.e. ch == ''.\n"
"    //\n"
"    // see also: Scripting API\n"
"    return -2;\n"
"}\n"
"</programlisting> The function <function>indent()</function> has three parameters: "
"<itemizedlist> "
"<listitem>"
"<para><literal>line</literal>: the line that has to be indented</para>"
"</listitem>"
" "
"<listitem>"
"<para><literal>indentWidth</literal>: the indentation width in number of spaces</para>"
"</listitem>"
" "
"<listitem>"
"<para><literal>ch</literal>: either a newline character (<literal>ch == '\\n'</literal>), the trigger character specified in <literal>triggerCharacters</literal> or empty if the user invoked the action <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Align</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.</para>"
"</listitem>"
" </itemizedlist>"
" The return value of the <function>indent()</function> function specifies how the line will be indented. If the return value is a simple integer number, it is interpreted as follows: "
"<itemizedlist> "
"<listitem>"
"<para>return value <literal>-2</literal>: do nothing</para>"
"</listitem>"
" "
"<listitem>"
"<para>return value <literal>-1</literal>: keep indentation (searches for previous non-blank line)</para>"
"</listitem>"
" "
"<listitem>"
"<para>return value <literal> 0</literal>: numbers &gt;= 0 specify the indentation depth in spaces</para>"
"</listitem>"
" </itemizedlist>"
" Alternatively, an array of two elements can be returned: "
"<itemizedlist> "
"<listitem>"
"<para><literal>return [ indent, align ];</literal></para>"
"</listitem>"
" </itemizedlist>"
" In this case, the first element is the indentation depth as above with the same meaning of the special values. However, the second element is an absolute value representing a column for <quote>alignment</quote>. If this value is higher than the indent value, the difference represents a number of spaces to be added after the indentation of the first parameter. Otherwise, the second number is ignored. Using tabs and spaces for indentation is often referred to as <quote>mixed mode</quote>."
msgstr ""
"Unha vez escrita a cabeceira, é hora de escribir o código que determina a lóxica do script de sangrado. O esqueleto básico do corpo ten o seguinte aspecto: <programlisting>\n"
"triggerCharacters = \"{}/:;\";\n"
"function indent(line, indentWidth, ch)\n"
"{\n"
"    // Esta función execútase para cada nova liña (ch == '\\n') e para\n"
"    // todos os caracteres indicados na variábel global triggerCharacters.\n"
"    // Cando se executa <menuchoice><guimenu>Utilidades</guimenu><guimenuitem>Aliñar</guimenuitem></menuchoice>\n"
"    // o parámetro ch chega baleiro, é dicir, ch == ''.\n"
"    //     // Vexa tamén a información da sección «API para scripts», máis abaixo.    return -2;\n"
"}\n"
"</programlisting>  A función <function>indent()</function> recibe tres parámetros: "
"<itemizedlist>   "
"<listitem>"
"<para><literal>line</literal>. A liña cuxo sangrado debe axustarse.</para>"
"</listitem>"
"   "
"<listitem>"
"<para><literal>indentWidth</literal>. A anchura do sangrado, medida en cantidade de espazos.</para>"
"</listitem>"
"   "
"<listitem>"
"<para><literal>ch</literal>. Un carácter de salto de liña (<literal>ch == '\\n'</literal>), o carácter disparador indicado en <literal>triggerCharacters</literal> ou unha cadea baleira se o usuario executou a acción <menuchoice><guimenu>Utilidades</guimenu><guimenuitem>Aliñar</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.</para>"
"</listitem>"
" </itemizedlist>"
"  O valor que devolva a función <function>indent()</function> determinará o sangrado da liña. De tratarse dun número enteiro, interpretarase da seguinte maneira: "
"<itemizedlist>   "
"<listitem>"
"<para><literal>-2</literal>. Non facer nada.</para>"
"</listitem>"
"   "
"<listitem>"
"<para><literal>-1</literal>. Manter o sangrado da primeira liña non baleira anterior á actual.</para>"
"</listitem>"
"   "
"<listitem>"
"<para><literal> 0</literal>. Os números positivos, incluído o 0, indican o nivel de sangrado a aplicar á liña, en espazos.</para>"
"</listitem>"
" </itemizedlist>"
" En vez dun enteiro, é posíbel devolver unha matriz de dous elementos: "
"<itemizedlist>   "
"<listitem>"
"<para><literal>[ sangrado, aliñación ];</literal></para>"
"</listitem>"
" </itemizedlist>"
" Neste caso, o primeiro elemento correspóndese co nivel de sangrado, igual que cando se devolve un número enteiro. Pola outra banda, o segundo elemento é un valor absoluto que representa a columna para a <quote>aliñación</quote>. Se o valor é superior ao valor de sangrado, a diferencia representa un número de espazos a engadir tras o sangrado do primeiro parámetro (o <quote>sangrado</quote>). En caso contrario, este segundo número ignorarase. Ao uso de tabulacións e espazos para o sangrado adoita chamárselle <quote>modo mixto</quote>."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Consider the following example: Assume using tabs to indent, and tab width is set to 4. Here, &lt;tab&gt; represents a tab and '.' a space: <programlisting>\n"
"1: &lt;tab&gt;&lt;tab&gt;foobar(\"hello\",\n"
"2: &lt;tab&gt;&lt;tab&gt;.......\"world\");\n"
"</programlisting> When indenting line 2, the <function>indent()</function> function returns [8, 15]. As result, two tabs are inserted to indent to column 8, and 7 spaces are added to align the second parameter under the first, so that it stays aligned if the file is viewed with a different tab width."
msgstr ""
"Digamos, por exemplo, que estamos a empregar tabulacións para o sangrado, e que a anchura das tabulacións é 4. Aquí, &lt;tab&gt; representa unha tabulación e «.» un espazo: <programlisting>\n"
"1: &lt;tab&gt;&lt;tab&gt;funcion(\"Ola,\",\n"
"2: &lt;tab&gt;&lt;tab&gt;....…\"mundo!\");\n"
"</programlisting> Ao estabelecerse o sangrado da liña 2, a función <function>indent()</function> devolve [8, 15]. Como resultado, insírense dúas tabulacións para levar o sangrado ata a columna 8, e 7 espazos para aliñar o segundo parámetro baixo o primeiro, de xeito que ambos permanezan aliñados independentemente da anchura que os distintos editores de textos cos que se abra o ficheiro empreguen para as tabulacións."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1205
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "A default KDE installation ships &kappname; with several indenters. The corresponding JavaScript source code can be found in <filename>$KDEDIR/share/apps/katepart/script</filename>."
msgid "A default &kde; installation ships &kappname; with several indenters. The corresponding JavaScript source code can be found in <filename>$<envar>XDG_DATA_DIRS</envar>/katepart5/script/indentation</filename>."
msgstr "A instalación predeterminada da colección de software de KDE fornece varios scripts de sangrado para &kappname;. O seu código fonte está dispoñíbel no cartafol <filename>$KDEDIR/share/apps/katepart/script</filename>."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1212
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Developing an indenter requires to reload the scripts to see whether the changes behave appropriately. Instead of restarting the application, simply switch to the command line and invoke the command <command>reload-scripts</command>."
msgid "Developing an indenter requires reloading the scripts to see whether the changes behave appropriately. Instead of restarting the application, simply switch to the command line and invoke the command <command>reload-scripts</command>."
msgstr "Ao desenvolver un script de sangrado, é necesario recargar os scripts para comprobar se os cambios funcionan como se espera. En vez de reiniciar o aplicativo, é posíbel recargalos empregando a orde <command>reload-scripts</command> desde a liña de ordes."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
