#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1250
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Command Line Script Header"
msgstr "A cabeceira do script da liña de ordes"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1251
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "The header of the file <filename>javascript.js</filename> is embedded in a comment and is of the following form <programlisting>\n"
#| "/* kate-script\n"
#| " * name: JavaScript\n"
#| " * author: Example Name &lt;example.name@some.address.org&gt;\n"
#| " * license: BSD\n"
#| " * revision: 1\n"
#| " * kate-version: 3.4\n"
#| " * type: indentation\n"
#| " * required-syntax-style: javascript\n"
#| " * indent-languages: javascript\n"
#| " * priority: 0\n"
#| " * i18n-catalog: mycatalog\n"
#| " *\n"
#| " * A line without colon ':' stops header parsing. That is, you can add optional\n"
#| " * text here such as a detailed license.\n"
#| " */\n"
#| "</programlisting> Each entry is explained in detail now:"
msgid ""
"The header of each command line script is embedded in JSON at the beginning of the script as follows: <programlisting>\n"
"var katescript = {\n"
"    \"author\": \"Example Name &lt;example.name@some.address.org&gt;\",\n"
"    \"license\": \"LGPLv2+\",\n"
"    \"revision\": 1,\n"
"    \"kate-version\": \"5.1\",\n"
"    \"functions\": [\"sort\", \"moveLinesDown\"],\n"
"    \"actions\": [\n"
"        {   \"function\": \"sort\",\n"
"            \"name\": \"Sort Selected Text\",\n"
"            \"category\": \"Editing\",\n"
"            \"interactive\": \"false\"\n"
"        },\n"
"        {   \"function\": \"moveLinesDown\",\n"
"            \"name\": \"Move Lines Down\",\n"
"            \"category\": \"Editing\",\n"
"            \"shortcut\": \"Ctrl+Shift+Down\",\n"
"            \"interactive\": \"false\"\n"
"        }\n"
"    ]\n"
"}; // kate-script-header, must be at the start of the file without comments\n"
"</programlisting> Each entry is explained in detail now:"
msgstr ""
"A cabeceira do ficheiro <filename>javascript.js</filename> escríbese nun comentario e ten a seguinte forma: <programlisting>\n"
"/* kate-script\n"
" * name: JavaScript\n"
" * author: Rosalía de Castro &lt;rosaliadecastro@example.com&gt;\n"
" * license: BSD\n"
" * revision: 1\n"
" * kate-version: 3.4\n"
" * type: indentation\n"
" * required-syntax-style: javascript\n"
" * indent-languages: javascript\n"
" * priority: 0\n"
" * i18n-catalog: catálogo_persoal\n"
" *\n"
" * A partir da primeira liña sen dous puntos («:») remata a análise\n"
" * da cabeceira, polo que pode empregar o comentario para\n"
" * texto adicional, como por exemplo detalles sobre a licencia\n"
" * do script.\n"
" */\n"
"</programlisting> A continuación explícanse punto por punto todas as entradas definidas na cabeceira:"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1259
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "<literal>license</literal> [optional]: Short form of the license, such as BSD or LGPLv3."
msgid "<literal>license</literal> [optional]: Short form of the license, such as BSD License or LGPLv2."
msgstr "<literal>license</literal> (opcional). Abreviatura da licenza. Por exemplo: BSD ou LGPLv3."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1262
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "<literal>functions</literal> [required]: Comma separated list of commands in the script."
msgid "<literal>functions</literal> [required]: JSON array of commands in the script."
msgstr "<literal>functions</literal> (obrigatorio). Lista de ordes definidas no script, separadas por comas."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1263
#, no-c-format
msgid "<literal>actions</literal> [optional]: JSON Array of JSON objects that defines the actions that appear in the application menu. Detailed information is provided in the section <link linkend=\"advanced-editing-tools-commandline\">Binding Shortcuts</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1267
#, no-c-format
msgid "Since the value of <literal>functions</literal> is a JSON array, a single script is able to contain an arbitrary number of command line commands. Each function is available through &kappname;'s <link linkend=\"advanced-editing-tools-commandline\">built-in command line</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1275
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Script Source Code"
msgstr "Código"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1277
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
