"// required katepart js libraries, e.g. range.js if you use Range\n"
"require (\"range.js\");\n"
"\n"
"function &lt;name&gt;(arg1, arg2, ...)\n"
"{\n"
"    // ... implementation, see also: Scripting API\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"function &lt;nome&gt;(arg1, arg2, …)\n"
"{\n"
"    // Código.\n"
"    // Vexa tamén a información da sección «API para scripts», máis abaixo.\n"
"}"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1286
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid ""
#| "Arguments in the command line are passed to the function as <parameter>arg1</parameter>, <parameter>arg2</parameter>, etc. In order to provide documentation for each command, simply implement the '<function>help</function>' function as follows: <programlisting>\n"
#| "function help(cmd)\n"
#| "{\n"
#| "    if (cmd == \"sort\") {\n"
#| "        return i18n(\"Sort the selected text.\");\n"
#| "    } else if (cmd == \"...\") {\n"
#| "        // ...\n"
#| "    }\n"
#| "}\n"
#| "</programlisting> Executing <command>help sort</command> in the command line then calls this help function with the argument <parameter>cmd</parameter> set to the given command, i.e. <parameter>cmd == \"sort\"</parameter>. &kappname; then presents the returned text as documentation to the user. Make sure to <link linkend=\"advanced-editing-tools-scripting-api-i18n\">translate the strings</link>."
msgid ""
"Arguments in the command line are passed to the function as <parameter>arg1</parameter>, <parameter>arg2</parameter>, etc. In order to provide documentation for each command, simply implement the '<function>help</function>' function as follows: <programlisting>\n"
"function help(cmd)\n"
"{\n"
"    if (cmd == \"sort\") {\n"
"        return i18n(\"Sort the selected text.\");\n"
"    } else if (cmd == \"...\") {\n"
"        // ...\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"</programlisting> Executing <command>help sort</command> in the command line then calls this help function with the argument <parameter>cmd</parameter> set to the given command, &ie; <parameter>cmd == \"sort\"</parameter>. &kappname; then presents the returned text as documentation to the user. Make sure to <link linkend=\"dev-scripting-api-i18n\">translate the strings</link>."
msgstr ""
"Os argumentos da liña de ordes envíanse ás funcións como <parameter>arg1</parameter>, <parameter>arg2</parameter>, etc. Para fornecer documentación para as ordes, defina a función «<function>help</function>» da seguinte maneira: <programlisting>\n"
"function help(cmd)\n"
"{\n"
"    if (cmd == \"sort\") {\n"
"        return i18n(\"Ordenar o texto seleccionado.\");\n"
"    } else if (cmd == \"…\") {\n"
"        // …\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"</programlisting> Ao executar <command>help sort</command> na liña de ordes, chámase a esta función co argumento <parameter>cmd</parameter> contendo o nome do parámetro (<parameter>cmd == \"sort\"</parameter>). &kappname; presenta entón o texto devolto como documentación, que o usuario pode ler. Asegúrese de <link linkend=\"advanced-editing-tools-scripting-api-i18n\">internacionalizar as cadeas</link>."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1301
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Developing a command line script requires to reload the scripts to see whether the changes behave appropriately. Instead of restarting the application, simply switch to the command line and invoke the command <command>reload-scripts</command>."
msgid "Developing a command line script requires reloading the scripts to see whether the changes behave appropriately. Instead of restarting the application, simply switch to the command line and invoke the command <command>reload-scripts</command>."
msgstr "Ao desenvolver un script da liña de ordes, é necesario recargar os scripts para comprobar se os cambios funcionan como se espera. En vez de reiniciar o aplicativo, é posíbel recargalos empregando a orde <command>reload-scripts</command> desde a liña de ordes."

