#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1357
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "To extend existing prototypes like <classname>Cursor</classname> or <classname>Range</classname>, the recommended way is to <emphasis>not</emphasis> modify the global <filename>*.js</filename> files. Instead, create a <filename>*.js</filename> file in the local folder that is being executed later than the <filename>05_cursor.js</filename> and then change the <classname>Cursor</classname> prototype in JavaScript."
msgid "To extend existing prototypes like <classname>Cursor</classname> or <classname>Range</classname>, the recommended way is to <emphasis>not</emphasis> modify the global <filename>*.js</filename> files. Instead, change the <classname>Cursor</classname> prototype in JavaScript after the <filename>cursor.js</filename> is included into your script via <literal>require</literal>."
msgstr "Para estender prototipos xa definidos, coma <classname>Cursor</classname> ou <classname>Range</classname>, recoméndase <emphasis>non</emphasis> modificar os ficheiros <filename>*.js</filename> globais (os do cartafol <filename>$KDEDIR/share/apps/katepart/api</filename>), senón crear un ficheiro <filename>*.js</filename> no cartafol local (<filename>$KDEHOME/share/apps/katepart/api</filename>) que se execute máis tarde que o ficheiro <filename>05_cursor.js</filename>, e entón cambiar o prototipo <classname>Cursor</classname> mediante JavaScript."

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1366
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cursors and Ranges"
msgstr "Cursores e intervalos"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1368
#, no-c-format
msgid "As &kappname; is a text editor, all the scripting API is based on cursors and ranges whenever possible. A Cursor is a simple <literal>(line, column)</literal> tuple representing a text position in the document. A Range spans text from a starting cursor position to an ending cursor position. The API is explained in detail in the next sections."
msgstr "Dado que &kappname; é un editor de texto, toda a súa API para scripts está baseada en cursores e intervalos, dentro do posíbel. Un cursor (<literal>Cursor</literal>) é unha lista de parellas <literal>(liña, columna)</literal> que representa unha posición no texto dun documento. Un intervalo (<literal>Range</literal>) é o texto entre un cursor inicial e un cursor final. As seguintes seccións explican en detalle o contido da API."

