#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1695
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "In order to support full localization, there are several functions to translate strings in scripts, namely <literal>i18n</literal>, <literal>i18nc</literal>, <literal>i18np</literal> and <literal>i18ncp</literal>. These functions behave exactly like <ulink url=\"http://techbase.kde.org/Development/Tutorials/Localization/i18n\"> KDE's translation functions</ulink>."
msgid "In order to support full localization, there are several functions to translate strings in scripts, namely <literal>i18n</literal>, <literal>i18nc</literal>, <literal>i18np</literal> and <literal>i18ncp</literal>. These functions behave exactly like <ulink url=\"https://techbase.kde.org/Development/Tutorials/Localization/i18n\"> &kde;'s translation functions</ulink>."
msgstr "Para permitir a localización dos scripts, existen diversas funcións: <literal>i18n</literal>, <literal>i18nc</literal>, <literal>i18np</literal> and <literal>i18ncp</literal>. Estas funcións compórtanse exactamente como as <ulink url=\"http://techbase.kde.org/Development/Tutorials/Localization/i18n\">funcións de internacionalización de KDE</ulink>."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1702
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "The translation functions translate the wrapped strings through KDE's translation system to the language used in the application. Strings in scripts being developed in the official &kappname; sources are automatically extracted and translatable. In other words, as a &kappname; developer you do not have to bother with message extraction and translation. However, for 3rd-party scripts developed outside of KDE, you have to extract and translate the messages yourself. Along with your scripts you have to also distribute a translation catalog, that includes all translated strings. Further, your script header then must explicitly state the catalog to load by specifying <literal>i18n-catalog</literal>."
msgid "The translation functions translate the wrapped strings through &kde;'s translation system to the language used in the application. Strings in scripts being developed in the official &kappname; sources are automatically extracted and translatable. In other words, as a &kappname; developer you do not have to bother with message extraction and translation. It should be noted though, that the translation only works inside the &kde; infrastructure, &ie;, new strings in 3rd-party scripts developed outside of &kde; are not translated. Therefore, please consider contributing your scripts to &kate; such that proper translation is possible."
msgstr "As funcións de internacionalización utilizan o sistema de tradución de KDE para fornecer a versión das cadeas na lingua na que se executa o aplicativo. As cadeas dos scripts desenvolvidos na versión oficial de &kappname; extráense de maneira automática e póñense a disposición dos tradutores. É dicir, os desenvolvedores de &kappname; non teñen que preocuparse das extracción das mensaxes nin da súa tradución. Porén, no caso dos scripts de terceiros desenvolvidos fóra do paraugas de KDE, deberá extraer e traducir vostede mesmo as mensaxes. Ademais, a cabeceira do seu script deberá indicar o nome do catálogo coas mensaxes traducidas mediante a entrada <literal>i18n-catalog</literal>."

#. Tag: synopsis
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1714
#, no-c-format
msgid "void i18n(<parameter>String <replaceable>text</replaceable></parameter>, <replaceable>arg1</replaceable>, ...);"
msgstr "void i18n(<parameter>String <replaceable>texto</replaceable></parameter>, <replaceable>argumento1</replaceable>, …);"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1715
#, no-c-format
msgid "Translates <replaceable>text</replaceable> into the language used by the application. The arguments <replaceable>arg1</replaceable>, ..., are optional and used to replace the placeholders <literal>%1</literal>, <literal>%2</literal>, etc."
msgstr "Imprime o <replaceable>texto</replaceable> no idioma do aplicativo, de estar dispoñíbel. Os argumentos <replaceable>argumento1</replaceable>, …, son opcionais e empréganse para substituír as marcas <literal>%1</literal>, <literal>%2</literal>, etc. Estas marcas inclúense no <replaceable>texto</replaceable> para indicar as posicións nas que se inserirán os parámetros na cadea final. Estes parámetros non se traducirán, se ben as traducións do <replaceable>texto</replaceable> terán total liberdade para cambiar a posición na que aparecen."

#. Tag: synopsis
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1722
#, no-c-format
msgid "void i18nc(<parameter>String <replaceable>context</replaceable></parameter>, <parameter>String <replaceable>text</replaceable></parameter>, <replaceable>arg1</replaceable>, ...);"
msgstr "void i18nc(<parameter>String <replaceable>contexto</replaceable></parameter>, <parameter>String <replaceable>texto</replaceable></parameter>, <replaceable>argumento1</replaceable>, …);"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1723
#, no-c-format
msgid "Translates <replaceable>text</replaceable> into the language used by the application. Additionally, the string <replaceable>context</replaceable> is visible to translators so they can provide a better translation. The arguments <replaceable>arg1</replaceable>, ..., are optional and used to replace the placeholders <literal>%1</literal>, <literal>%2</literal>, etc."
msgstr "Imprime o <replaceable>texto</replaceable> no idioma do aplicativo, de estar dispoñíbel. Ademais, a cadea de texto <replaceable>context</replaceable> poderán vela os tradutores, para poder fornecer mellores traducións. Os argumentos <replaceable>argumento1</replaceable>, …, son opcionais e empréganse para substituír as marcas <literal>%1</literal>, <literal>%2</literal>, etc."

#. Tag: synopsis
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1732
#, no-c-format
msgid "void i18np(<parameter>String <replaceable>singular</replaceable></parameter>, <parameter>String <replaceable>plural</replaceable></parameter>, <parameter>int <replaceable>number</replaceable></parameter>, <replaceable>arg1</replaceable>, ...);"
msgstr "void i18np(<parameter>String <replaceable>singular</replaceable></parameter>, <parameter>String <replaceable>plural</replaceable></parameter>, <parameter>int <replaceable>número</replaceable></parameter>, <replaceable>argumento1</replaceable>, …);"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1733
#, no-c-format
msgid "Translates either <replaceable>singular</replaceable> or <replaceable>plural</replaceable> into the language used by the application, depending on the given <replaceable>number</replaceable>. The arguments <replaceable>arg1</replaceable>, ..., are optional and used to replace the placeholders <literal>%1</literal>, <literal>%2</literal>, etc."
msgstr "Imprime a versión <replaceable>singular</replaceable> ou <replaceable>plural</replaceable> do <replaceable>texto</replaceable> —dependendo do <replaceable>número</replaceable>— no idioma do aplicativo, de estar dispoñíbel. Os argumentos <replaceable>argumento1</replaceable>, …, son opcionais e empréganse para substituír as marcas <literal>%1</literal>, <literal>%2</literal>, etc. Estas marcas inclúense no <replaceable>texto</replaceable> para indicar as posicións nas que se inserirán os parámetros na cadea final. Estes parámetros non se traducirán, se ben as traducións do <replaceable>texto</replaceable> terán total liberdade para cambiar a posición na que aparecen."

#. Tag: synopsis
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1742
#, no-c-format
msgid "void i18ncp(<parameter>String <replaceable>context</replaceable></parameter>, <parameter>String <replaceable>singular</replaceable></parameter>, <parameter>String <replaceable>plural</replaceable></parameter>, <parameter>int <replaceable>number</replaceable></parameter>, <replaceable>arg1</replaceable>, ...);"
msgstr "void i18ncp(<parameter>String <replaceable>contexto</replaceable></parameter>, <parameter>String <replaceable>singular</replaceable></parameter>, <parameter>String <replaceable>plural</replaceable></parameter>, <parameter>int<replaceable>número</replaceable></parameter>, <replaceable>argumento1</replaceable>, …);"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1743
#, no-c-format
msgid "Translates either <replaceable>singular</replaceable> or <replaceable>plural</replaceable> into the language used by the application, depending on the given <replaceable>number</replaceable>. Additionally, the string <replaceable>context</replaceable> is visible to translators so they can provide a better translation. The arguments <replaceable>arg1</replaceable>, ..., are optional and used to replace the placeholders <literal>%1</literal>, <literal>%2</literal>, etc."
msgstr "Imprime a versión <replaceable>singular</replaceable> ou <replaceable>plural</replaceable> do <replaceable>texto</replaceable> —dependendo do <replaceable>número</replaceable>— no idioma do aplicativo, de estar dispoñíbel. Ademais, a cadea de texto do <replaceable>context</replaceable> poderán vela os tradutores para fornecer unha mellor tradución. Os argumentos <replaceable>argumento1</replaceable>, …, son opcionais e empréganse para substituír as marcas <literal>%1</literal>, <literal>%2</literal>, etc."

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1757
#, no-c-format
msgid "The View API"
msgstr "A API da vista"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1758
#, no-c-format
msgid "Whenever a script is being executed, there is a global variable <quote><literal>view</literal></quote> representing the current active editor view. The following is a list of all available View functions."
msgstr "Ao executarse un script, o ambiente de execución contén unha variábel global, <quote><literal>view</literal></quote>, que representa a vista do editor actual. A variábel fornece os métodos da seguinte lista."

#. Tag: synopsis
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1765
#, no-c-format
msgid "<function>Cursor view.cursorPosition()</function>"
msgstr "<function>Cursor view.cursorPosition()</function>"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: development.docbook:1766
#, no-c-format
msgid "Returns the current cursor position in the view."
msgstr "Devolve a posición actual do cursor na vista."

